{title: Dear Lord and Father of Mankind}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Dear [C]Lord and [F]Father [C]of man[C]kind
Forg[Dm]ive our [F]foolish [G]ways[**]
Re[F]clothe us [F]in our [G]rightful [G]mind
In [Am]purer l[F]ives Thy s[G]ervice [Em]find
In [C]deeper [F]reverence [G]praise[**]. In [Dm]deeper [F]reverence [C]praise[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
In [C]simple [F]trust like [C]theirs who [C]heard
Be[Dm]side the [F]Syrian [G]sea[**]
The [F]gracious [F]calling [G]of the [G]Lord
Let [Am]us, like [F]them, wit[G]hout a [Em]word
Rise [C]up and [F]follow [G]Thee[**]. Rise [Dm]up and [F]follow [C]Thee.[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [C]Sabbath [F]rest by [C]Gali[C]lee
O [Dm]calm of [F]hills a[G]bove[**]
Where [F]Jesus [F]knelt to [G]share with [G]Thee
The [Am]silence [F]of e[G]terni[Em]ty
In[C]terpre[F]ted by [G]love[**]! In[Dm]terpre[F]ted by [C]love![**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
With [C]that deep [F]hush sub[C]duing [C]all
Our [Dm]words and [F]works that [G]drown[**]
The [F]tender [F]whisper [G]of Thy [G]call
As [Am]noiseless [F]let Thy [G]blessing [Em]fall
As [C]fell Thy [F]manna [G]down[**]. As [Dm]fell Thy [F]manna [C]down[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 5}
Drop [C]Thy still [F]dews of [C]quiet[C]ness
Till [Dm]all our [F]strivings [G]cease[**]
Take [F]from our [F]souls the [G]strain and [G]stress
And [Am]let our [F]ordered [G]lives con[Em]fess
The [C]beauty [F]of Thy [G]peace[**]. The [Dm]beauty [F]of Thy [C]peace[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 6}
Breathe [C]through the [F]heats of [C]our de[C]sire
Thy [Dm]coolness [F]and Thy [G]balm[**]
Let [F]sense be [F]dumb, let [G]flesh re[G]tire
Speak [Am]through the [F]earthquake, [G]wind, and [Em]fire
O [C]still, small [F]voice of [G]calm[**]. O [Dm]still, small [F]voice of [C]calm[**].
{end_of_verse}
